Ularn 1.6.3a should contain the following files:

Filename                Description
--------                -----------
README                  it's the readme (branch notes, then the original Readme.txt)
README.spoilers         spoiler guide from Phil Cordier's web site
INSTALL                 build and installation instructions
CHANGES.text            version history
MANIFEST                this list
LICENSE                 GNU General Public License, version 2
COPYRIGHT               authorship, and which modules are NOT GPL
BSDLicense.txt          BSD license template, as shipped in the distribution

data/                   run-time files, read from ./lib by the engine
  Uhelp                 help file
  Umaps                 predefined dungeon maps
  Ufortune              fortune cookie messages

src/                    game engine
  ularn.c               setup (ULarnSetup) and command dispatch
  ularn_game.c/.h       game data and options
  ularn_ask.c/.h        prompts, as callbacks
  ularn_win.c/.h        headless front end: state getters and JSON output
  MemoryFile.c/.h       in-memory file used for save games
  action.c/.h           player actions
  diag.c/.h             diagnostic dump
  dungeon.c/.h          dungeon levels
  dungeon_obj.c/.h      static dungeon objects (altars, thrones, fountains...)
  fortune.c/.h          fortune cookies
  header.h              common macros
  help.c/.h             help file and welcome screen
  itm.c/.h              item definitions and names
  monster.c/.h          monsters
  object.c/.h           what the player finds when moving onto a square
  patchlevel.h          version and patch level
  player.c/.h           the player
  potion.c/.h           potions
  savegame.c/.h         save and restore
  saveutils.c/.h        save file utilities
  scores.c/.h           scoreboard
  scroll.c/.h           scrolls and books
  show.c/.h             item names and inventory lists
  spell.c/.h            spells
  sphere.c/.h           spheres of annihilation
  store.c/.h            the home level: DND store, bank, college, LRS, etc.
  config.h              LIBDIR
  build.sh, build.bat   Emscripten build commands (reference)
